1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,638
So now you know on parent's
day, when we have parents here,

2
00:00:04,638 --> 00:00:05,939
we had the two sheets of glass.

3
00:00:05,939 --> 00:00:07,140
One is called annealed.

4
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:10,544
It just means it's not
tempered, and the baseball

5
00:00:10,544 --> 00:00:13,013
was supposed to break it.

6
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:15,182
It didn't.

7
00:00:15,182 --> 00:00:16,884
Peter's got very
good annealed glass.

8
00:00:16,884 --> 00:00:19,353
He's the one that gave
us those big sheets.

9
00:00:19,353 --> 00:00:22,789
And it breaks into these
huge, dangerous shards.

10
00:00:22,789 --> 00:00:23,390
Thanks, Peter.

11
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:25,425
Take care.

12
00:00:25,425 --> 00:00:26,860
Oh yeah, thank you.

13
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:30,230
[APPLAUSE]

14
00:00:33,634 --> 00:00:37,938
If you notice, the tempered
glass, we tried to break it.

15
00:00:37,938 --> 00:00:39,840
It also doesn't break.

16
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:42,442
It was supposed to be the
only one that didn't break.

17
00:00:42,442 --> 00:00:44,611
But then you take a
little hammer at the edge

18
00:00:44,611 --> 00:00:47,447
and you just lightly tap
the edge and the whole thing

19
00:00:47,447 --> 00:00:47,948
breaks.

20
00:00:47,948 --> 00:00:48,548
Why?

21
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:52,252
Because it's got so
much built-in stress.

22
00:00:52,252 --> 00:00:54,655
It's got all this
compressive stress,

23
00:00:54,655 --> 00:00:58,025
and the edge isn't
protecting that.

24
00:00:58,025 --> 00:01:01,094
The edge of that tempered glass
isn't protecting the stress.

25
00:01:01,094 --> 00:01:03,130
So when I just dig
in a little bit,

26
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:07,067
it's able to all crack
and release that stress.

27
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,936
So that's what
happened on family day.

28
00:01:08,936 --> 00:01:10,170
Here's a high-speed video.

29
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:12,005
These are two guys from Corning.

30
00:01:12,005 --> 00:01:14,107
And we can listen to this.

31
00:01:14,107 --> 00:01:14,775
[VIDEO PLAYBACK]

32
00:01:14,775 --> 00:01:16,075
They're actually pretty cool.
